# Line endings are git's business, not each machine's.
#
# Without this, normalisation hangs on whatever `core.autocrlf` each contributor
# happens to have. On 13.08.2026 one file went into history with `CR CR LF` on
# sixteen lines; git then marked that one file of 356 as not text, stopped
# normalising it, and rewrote the whole of it in a single merge, so every line of
# it was attributed to that merge and the next person to touch it on Linux would
# have conflicted on all 258 lines. One line here closes the class rather than
# the instance.
* text=auto

# Binaries, said out loud so nothing tries to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
